ray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/989021-ever-used-creepypastas-scp-etc-in-your-games?p=989033#post989033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are these things of which you speak?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creepy Pastas are basically internet horror stories. the SPC foundation is a sort of fan based work, its a &quot;Technocracy&quot; sort of group that catalogs paranormal entities. The main catch about the SCP is that anyone can write one of these downs. google some of em","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T16:48:11-07:00","id":989072,"title":"","content":"If you'll divert to the CofD for a second, I have used the life-twisting Sarkic Cults as antagonists. Very Tzmisce-like, they are, with extra Cthulhu. Also a surviving Daevite (a cruel human subspecies that was supposed to have died out in primordial times, but one of their sorcerers made a history book that extends the period of their existence if fed with blood, with the hope of one day the empire living forever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-17-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T17:16:39-07:00","id":989080,"title":"","content":"I guess it's SCP as in special containment procedure...I never thought about using them.<br /> <br /> There's the SCP foundation and the other rival faction that could be seen as Techno vs Pentex.<br /> <br /> Other than that...there was two SCPs that could be interesting (I don't remember their id):<br /> - The one that looks like a dark shadow and builds its own dark realm seems like an Abyssal creature summoned by Obtenebration straight from Hell.<br /> - And the insect SCP that stalks you while staying out of your FoV...that one was creepy.<br /> <br /> But the best and creepiest one would be the cloning machine. You put in some Hit-marks, then you chose the &quot;improve&quot; option...*chills*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:12:59-07:00","id":989312,"title":"","content":"There was a large set of CreepyPasta's I read once that first introduced me to the idea that the interstate system is built on Lay Lines; I have twisted that around in my head and have intents to use that some day in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:18:24-07:00","id":989383,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can use creepypasta, but you should be careful because if you add too many new monsters, the setting becomes a &quot;Jurasic Park&quot; for gothic monsters, like that tv series where heroes have to kill a different enemy each episode. <br /> <br /> But you also play with ambiguity. Maybe the new monsters are only variations of known creatures, like the chimeras or the bane spirtis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:07:02-07:00","id":989563,"title":"","content":"If you're not playing core CoD/H:tV in a creepypasta setting you're doing it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:14:16-07:00","id":989667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/989021-ever-used-creepypastas-scp-etc-in-your-games?p=989383#post989383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you can use creepypasta, but you should be careful because if you add too many new monsters, the setting becomes a &quot;Jurasic Park&quot; for gothic monsters, like that tv series where heroes have to kill a different enemy each episode.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually see no problem with this at all about adding new monsters which actually makes the setting more diverse and unpredictable to make things more interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/989021-ever-used-creepypastas-scp-etc-in-your-games?p=989383#post989383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you also play with ambiguity. Maybe the new monsters are only variations of known creatures, like the chimeras or the bane spirtis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course that would only make things more boringly predictable if you do that and plus alot of cultural appropriation (if we're using folkloric or even other deities) would happen which end up being problematic in the end.<br /> <br /> It's often very annoying to see that people having hard time grasping diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 10-18-2016, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T08:13:26-07:00","id":989882,"title":"","content":"The SCP items are extremely useful as game material but you have to determine their relevance. In a Hunter game, your approach to these items is the same as the SCP Foundation - keep people safe. You might also try to destroy them which the Foundation ordinarily doesn't, but in general, you can use them as is.<br /> <br /> For other games, how do they fit into that world? For example - there's an SCP that's a lake filled with a red liquid that may or may not be blood, from which horrors rise and attack; a Foundation outpost surrounds it to keep them from getting out. If you're playing Vampire, why do vampires in particular care? Maybe the lake is really Vitae, and that's why the Foundation can't identify it as normal blood. Maybe the lake itself is a horribly powerful Tzimisce experimenting with fleshcrafting and releasing its creation. Now that you've added on vampire-ness to the base SCP, you're ready to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T05:10:42-08:00","id":1005312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/989021-ever-used-creepypastas-scp-etc-in-your-games?p=989882#post989882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For other games, how do they fit into that world? For example - there's an SCP that's a lake filled with a red liquid that may or may not be blood, from which horrors rise and attack; a Foundation outpost surrounds it to keep them from getting out. If you're playing Vampire, why do vampires in particular care? Maybe the lake is really Vitae, and that's why the Foundation can't identify it as normal blood. Maybe the lake itself is a horribly powerful Tzimisce experimenting with fleshcrafting and releasing its creation. Now that you've added on vampire-ness to the base SCP, you're ready to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would have to be an ancient childe of Tzimisce itself to pull that off wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> Also, how does the lake deal with the daylight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:59:02-08:00","id":1005574,"title":"","content":"Variant of the <i>Coccoon</i> Vicissitude power that makes the uppermost layers of blood into an opaque protective barrier to blot out the sun's rays?<br /> <br /> Actually if a storyteller let a Tzimisce sorcerer learn Sanguinus himself and use it on Blood Brothers he created, it could theoretically be done with Vicissitude 5, Sanguinus 5, and Way of Water 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 11-20-2016, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}